b2=A.a([A.w(h8,"In Hong Kong Cantonese Mahjong, the dealer (East) has NO special payment bonus. Whether dealer or not, winners and payers follow the same half-fire rules.",h9,h9),A.w(h8,"Dealer rotation: If East wins (by discard or self-draw), they stay as dealer for the next hand (\u9023\u838a). If East does not win, the dealer position rotates clockwise to the next player.",h9,h9),A.w(h8,"A full game = 4 rounds (East, South, West, North). Each round has at least 4 hands (one per dealer). Minimum 16 hands per full game!",h9,h9),A.w(h8,"Being dealer is still important: you get the first draw and you keep the dealer seat as long as you win. But there is no extra 50% payment - that rule does NOT apply in standard Hong Kong play.",h9,h9)],n5)
